      "source": "The Očhéthi Šakówiŋ, the Seven Council Fires: the Dakota in the woodlands, the Nakota and the Lakota out on the plains as the horse carried them west after 1700. Drawn to the act of February 1877 that took the Black Hills. The United States claims this ground from the Louisiana Purchase of 1803 and holds very little of it until the 1870s, which is the gap this layer exists to show." }
